    "result_text": "All tests pass. The only test classes are the acceptance tests (`AuditLogCapture` is a helper), and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI changed telephone handling to store and compare numbers in **E.164** form.\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Rewrote `normalizeTelephone` to produce E.164: strips spaces/dashes/brackets; keeps a leading `+` and its country code when present, otherwise assumes `+61` and drops a single leading `0` from the national digits; requires 8\u201315 digits after the `+`, throwing `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (\u2192 400) otherwise. `\"0412 345 678\"` \u2192 `\"+61412345678\"`.\n- Added `toE164OrNull` helper and switched `rejectDuplicateTelephone` to compare **E.164 values** (existing owners' telephones are best-effort normalized to E.164 before comparison) instead of stripped 10-digit strings.\n- `updateOwner` now normalizes the telephone the same way, so stored values stay consistent with the new entity constraint.\n\n**`Owner.java`**\n- Replaced the old `@Digits(integer=10)` + `@Pattern(\"^[0-9]{10}$\")` constraints with `@Pattern(\"^\\\\+[0-9]{8,15}$\")` (E.164), and dropped the now-unused `@Digits` import.\n\n**`openapi.yml`**\n- Updated the `telephone` field description and example to describe the E.164 normalization.\n\nThe `VARCHAR(20)` DB columns already accommodate the \u226416-char E.164 strings, so no schema change was needed. All 3 acceptance tests (national\u2192E.164, explicit country code kept, unformattable rejected with 400) pass.",
